  "notes": "A medical term composed of {内|ない} (internal) and {服|ふく} (take, ingest). Contrasts with {外用|がいよう} (external application) and {注射|ちゅうしゃ} (injection). Common in medical and pharmacy contexts.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {内服薬|ないふくやく}: oral medication\n- {内服|ないふく}する: to take medicine orally\n- {内服|ないふく}{治療|ちりょう}: oral treatment\n- {内服|ないふく}{液|えき}: liquid oral medicine\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {服用|ふくよう}: taking medicine — more general and common; does not specify the route\n- {外用|がいよう}: external application — the counterpart for topical medicines\n- {経口|けいこう}: oral (route of administration) — more technical medical term",
